"""brando shared fonts — one copy of a face the fleet vendors three times.

`SpaceGrotesk-Medium.ttf`, `SpaceGrotesk-SemiBold.ttf` and `OFL.txt` were
md5-identical in fastverk/brand, tomato-bazel/brand and meridian-ux/brand: ~530 KB
of binary duplicated across three repos, with three separately-maintained
`exports_files` blocks (two of them byte-identical at 153 bytes) and three places
someone would have to remember to look when the licence question comes up.

Nothing about a libre typeface is brand content, so it lives here. A brand that
uses Space Grotesk depends on `@brando//fonts:space_grotesk` and deletes its copy;
a brand with its own licensed face keeps that face in its own repo, which is the
correct place for something whose licence is not OFL.

PROVENANCE. `SOURCES.json` records where each file came from, its size, and its
sha256 — the format aion/brand invented for its webfonts and the only provenance
record anywhere in the fleet. A vendored binary with no provenance is a licence
question nobody can answer later.
"""

package(default_visibility = ["//visibility:public"])

exports_files([
    "OFL.txt",
    "SOURCES.json",
    "SpaceGrotesk-Medium.ttf",
    "SpaceGrotesk-SemiBold.ttf",
])

# The pair a brand_mdbook_theme / brand_latex_class / brand_wordmark wants, plus
# the licence. The licence is IN the filegroup on purpose: an OFL face may be
# redistributed, and shipping the face without the licence is the one way to get
# that wrong.
filegroup(
    name = "space_grotesk",
    srcs = [
        "OFL.txt",
        "SpaceGrotesk-Medium.ttf",
        "SpaceGrotesk-SemiBold.ttf",
    ],
)

filegroup(
    name = "space_grotesk_medium",
    srcs = ["SpaceGrotesk-Medium.ttf"],
)

filegroup(
    name = "space_grotesk_semibold",
    srcs = ["SpaceGrotesk-SemiBold.ttf"],
)
